  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル教材。人物や出来事は架空の例であり、実在の事業・調査・実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A group of students prepared a short play for a school festival.",
          "ja": "生徒のグループは学校祭のため短い劇を準備した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Yuki had an important line near the end of the play.",
          "ja": "ユキには劇の終わり近くに重要なせりふがあった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She practiced saying the words quickly and clearly.",
          "ja": "言葉を速く明確に言う練習をした。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Her teacher asked her to try the same line in a different way.",
          "ja": "教師は同じせりふを別の方法で試すよう頼んだ。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "First, Yuki read the line without stopping.",
          "ja": "最初ユキは止まらずにせりふを読んだ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Then she waited for a moment before saying the final words.",
          "ja": "次に最後の言葉を言う前に少し待った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Her classmates listened to both versions.",
          "ja": "級友は両方の版を聞いた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They said the second version made the character seem more thoughtful.",
          "ja": "第二版は登場人物がより思慮深く見えると言った。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Yuki was surprised because the words were exactly the same.",
          "ja": "言葉はまったく同じだったためユキは驚いた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She began to notice the spaces between the words.",
          "ja": "言葉と言葉の間に気づき始めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Other students tried changing the speed of their own lines.",
          "ja": "他の生徒も自分のせりふの速さを変えてみた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They compared how the changes affected the scene.",
          "ja": "変化が場面にどう影響したか比較した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Before the festival, the group practiced again in front of a few friends.",
          "ja": "学校祭前、数人の友人の前で再び練習した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The friends explained which moments were easy to understand.",
          "ja": "どの場面が理解しやすかったか友人は説明した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The actors used this feedback to improve their performance.",
          "ja": "役者はこの意見を使い演技を改善した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They did not need to change the story itself.",
          "ja": "物語そのものを変える必要はなかった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Yuki learned that acting involves more than remembering words.",
          "ja": "演技には言葉を覚える以上のことが伴うとユキは学んだ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A short pause can help the audience understand a character's feelings.",
          "ja": "短い間は観客が人物の感情を理解する助けになり得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The timing of a line can be part of its meaning.",
          "ja": "せりふのタイミングは意味の一部になり得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Sometimes silence can speak as clearly as words.",
          "ja": "時に沈黙は言葉と同じくらい明確に語り得る。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
